  "guideP2": "Low potencies (3X–12X, 6C) are often repeated a few times a day. 30C is the most common strength for first aid and short-term complaints. 200C and 1M are high potencies, given less often and normally on a practitioner's advice.",
  "guideP3T": "How much and how often",
  "guideP3": "The amount per dose changes little with potency; the age group and how often it is repeated matter more. Stop when you feel better, and see a doctor if a complaint is severe, lasts, or keeps coming back.",
